{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"TAO","id":"267178019196633099","is_bot":0,"username":"dm_tao"},"author_id":"267178019196633099","channel_id":"732867492040540210","content":"Kairo, alone with his thoughts, looks out over the Thames from a lush veranda with potted ferns and statues honouring Britain's most famous explorers. He sighs and takes in the morning air, \"I can't wait to be somewhere that doesn't smell like... well, like whatever is so rank.\" He brings a kerchief to his nose as he stifles a gag. \"It just ain't natural.\" He picks up a few black and white pebbles that line the potted ferns and begins to target the hanging signs and drain spouts of the street below. With a thud and a ting, the targets ring out as they are struck lightly with a flicked pebble here and there. A shopkeep sticks his head out his door to see what the sound is. Kairo quickly ducks down to avoid being seen and chuckles quietly to himself. \"He he, that old codger almost saw me this time. Better head back to the museum, lots to do.\"","created_at":"2020-07-19T13:59:52.792000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"734409178394787880","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"BenevolentDM","id":"470420431841656833","is_bot":0,"username":"benevolentdm"},"author_id":"470420431841656833","channel_id":"732867492040540210","content":"Ozgur walks down the street on his way to work, dressed in his new uniform, he's quietly singing to himself an old maori folk tune he learned years ago \"macoway, cowetana~ Way, way cowetana...\"","created_at":"2020-07-19T15:46:31.921000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"734436018287149116","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Deleted User","id":"456226577798135808","is_bot":0,"username":"Deleted User"},"author_id":"456226577798135808","channel_id":"732867492040540210","content":"Shoga, approaches London from the Thames side and looks at the large settlement.  She is partially excited, partially afraid.  But her blood instincts tell her she should continue to at least 'see' this place as she will likely never return.","created_at":"2020-07-19T15:47:16.337000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"734436204581355581","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Deleted User","id":"456226577798135808","is_bot":0,"username":"Deleted User"},"author_id":"456226577798135808","channel_id":"732867492040540210","content":"Shoga, catches the briefest of a song melody carried on the wind from somewhere nearby, but she doesn't know.  She pauses, tries to see if she has heard it before.  Not having done so, she shrugs.  Adjusts her gear, and cloak and continues on looking at the variety of wares and goods being sold.","created_at":"2020-07-19T15:51:14.209000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"734437202288705556","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Deleted User","id":"456226577798135808","is_bot":0,"username":"Deleted User"},"author_id":"456226577798135808","channel_id":"732867492040540210","content":"The melody, lingers and Shoga is caught by a vision.  The street swims in front of her.  What there is of today blending of past and future events.  A fire, a riot, a mother carrying a babe in her arms.  Darkness, and light swirling together along with explosions.  Shoga being somewhat overwhelmed sways in her stance.  And just as quickly as it started the vision ends leaving Shoga slightly dazed.  Shaking her head to clear it, she continues down her lonely path.  Surrounded by people, yet very isolated.","created_at":"2020-07-19T16:10:03.314000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-19T16:29:14.351000Z","id":"734441938098585620","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
